Article 3 (Approval of and Reporting on Major Policy Matters, etc.)
(1) The heads of agencies shall obtain the Minister's prior approval for the following matters:
1. Enactment, amendment, or repeal of statutes or regulations;
2. Establishment of and changes to basic plans for major policies requiring a budget;
3. Establishment of and changes to plans for international cooperation;
4. Membership in international organizations or conclusion of international agreements.
(2) The heads of agencies shall report the following matters to the Minister in advance:
1. Matters concerning the amendment of organizational regulations;
2. Matters concerning their attendance at international conferences and overseas official trips;
3. Matters to be submitted to the State Council.
(3) The heads of agencies shall report to the Minister on matters in the following categories:
1. Common matters:
  (a) Implementation plans concerning directions issued by the President, Prime Minister, or Minister, and their implementation results;
  (b) Quarterly results of implementing major policies and plans and the results of analyses thereof;
  (c) Matters deemed particularly important among materials reported or submitted to the President, Prime Minister, and organizations directly under them, the National Assembly, the Board of Audit and Inspection, etc.;
  (d) Matters that have caused public controversy or are the subject of important civil petitions;
  (e) Important damage to agriculture or forests;
  (f) Important information concerning international cooperation proposed or received in relation to affairs under their jurisdiction;
  (g) Important results of testing and research projects;
  (h) Particularly important affairs of subordinate organizations.
2. Matters under the jurisdiction of the Rural Development Administration:
  (a) Establishment, issuance, and implementation of basic plans for rural guidance programs;
  (b) Establishment of and changes to basic plans for the development of agricultural science and technology;
  (c) Establishment, issuance, and implementation of basic plans for education and training.
3. Matters under the jurisdiction of the Korea Forest Service:
  (a) Establishment, implementation, and amendment of the Basic Forest Plan;
  (b) Long-term forecasts of demand and supply for forest resources and forest products;
  (c) Designation of mountain village promotion areas.
